(6185797, 911818, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> What a fun image!  Great wardrobe, and the flock wall is a wonderful detail.  Oddly, I''m ok with the upper body crop, but somehow the missing foot is disturbing.  And surely, with so much attention to detail, you could have found a more interesting footrest?  Nice, vibrant colors, but not a fan of the desat.  I honestly don''t think this image needed it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually there was no desat. The model''s skin (whether through makeup or natural) was white as were her leggings. But I truly appreciate your thoughtful comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: What a fun image!  Great wardrobe, and the flock wall is a wonderful detail.  Oddly, I''m ok with the upper body crop, but somehow the missing foot is disturbing.  And surely, with so much attention to detail, you could have found a more interesting footrest?  Nice, vibrant colors, but not a fan of the desat.  I honestly don''t think this image needed it.   Actually there was no desat. The model''s skin (whether through makeup or natural) was white as were her leggings. But I truly appreciate your thoughtful comment.', '2010-10-08 02:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6185798, 909961, 103032, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the self portrait.  I like these portraits with "hard" lighting and "hard" shadows.  Makes it a more interesting image, IMO.  Keep experimenting with lighting.</td>', 'Nice job on the self portrait.  I like these portraits with "hard" lighting and "hard" shadows.  Makes it a more interesting image, IMO.  Keep experimenting with lighting.', '2010-10-08 02:46:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6185800, 911986, 30214, '<td valign="top">lovely, with a feel of  distant and fading memory.</td>', 'lovely, with a feel of  distant and fading memory.', '2010-10-08 03:01:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(6185802, 912095, 30214, '<td valign="top">terrific and ominous. look more like a gravure than a photograph (and I mean it as a compliment)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-08 02:04:50.</i></td>', 'terrific and ominous. look more like a gravure than a photograph (and I mean it as a compliment)', '2010-10-08 03:04:03.000000', '2010-10-08 03:04:50.000000', 0),
(6185803, 908425, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> excellent geometry of light and shadows here, Paul. (I''m wondering whether you used a tripod or have very steady hands) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Two Cokin ND filters ND4+ND8, hand-held at about 1/2 sec I think (but I was leaning on a doorframe).  Square crop &amp; a touch of curves for contrast.  Nothing else in PP ... I don''t know how to use Photoshop &amp; don''t care to find out.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: excellent geometry of light and shadows here, Paul. (I''m wondering whether you used a tripod or have very steady hands)  Two Cokin ND filters ND4+ND8, hand-held at about 1/2 sec I think (but I was leaning on a doorframe).  Square crop & a touch of curves for contrast.  Nothing else in PP ... I don''t know how to use Photoshop & don''t care to find out.', '2010-10-08 03:04:15.000000', NULL, 0),
