(6186218, 911911, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by colorcarnival:</b></div><hr/><i> Lev this is flippin cool!  That hand replica is amazing.  What a clever idea - is this being used in some type of Halloween display?  What a wonderful concoction. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No Michelle, it was just some out of blue Friday night "experiment" at my friend''s house - he happened to have some dry ice and we started to look around to see what can we compose with it. Found a pomegranate, and a plaster hand :). I thought it could work as a dark-humored postcard for Rosh Hashanah (Jewish New Year): Pomegranate is one of symbolic foods for it along with apples and honey.</td>', 'Originally posted by colorcarnival: Lev this is flippin cool!  That hand replica is amazing.  What a clever idea - is this being used in some type of Halloween display?  What a wonderful concoction.  No Michelle, it was just some out of blue Friday night "experiment" at my friend''s house - he happened to have some dry ice and we started to look around to see what can we compose with it. Found a pomegranate, and a plaster hand :). I thought it could work as a dark-humored postcard for Rosh Hashanah (Jewish New Year): Pomegranate is one of symbolic foods for it along with apples and honey.', '2010-10-08 12:23:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6186225, 910235, 98339, '<td valign="top">Look at u!!   Excellent finish</td>', 'Look at u!!   Excellent finish', '2010-10-08 12:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6186231, 911491, 66515, '<td valign="top">Glad you enjoyed/are enjoying your stay in Alberta. The Rockies are indeed magical and each National Park in them shows a different look. <br/> <br/>Congratulations on your ribbon!<br/> <br/>eta: I saw in a previous post you were in one of Darwin Wiggett''s workshops. Was this also taken during one of them? (And I take it you aren''t in Rhode Island anymore?)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-08 11:52:12.</i></td>', 'Glad you enjoyed/are enjoying your stay in Alberta. The Rockies are indeed magical and each National Park in them shows a different look.  Congratulations on your ribbon! eta: I saw in a previous post you were in one of Darwin Wiggett''s workshops. Was this also taken during one of them? (And I take it you aren''t in Rhode Island anymore?)', '2010-10-08 12:50:55.000000', '2010-10-08 12:52:12.000000', 0),
