(6186631, 912018, 99392, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bohemka:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t know what blown highlights sldpixel is talking about. There are no blown highlights. And I don''t know what the problem is with there not being enough color... just because you called it Fall?<br/> <br/>I do agree the border is a bit weird though. Either go letterbox or equidistant all the way around (at least for voters); or better, no border at all, especially with a shot like this, which doesn''t need it.<br/> <br/>With a shot this good you want to go as big as possible, so scrap the border altogether. And a black border doesn''t help the scene. Sorry to go on about the border. It''s a great shot and should have done a hell of a lot better. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the feedback, Scott.  I''m just getting into photography (bought my first DSLR 2 months ago) and I certainly appreciate all the critiques.  I thought I had a decent shot here, but it seems to have been dismissed for certain reasons.  Ultimately I made a poor decision with the title (hey I''m from Southern California, so this looks very much like fall to me), as well as the choice for a border.  Again, these are learning curves for me and I''ll definitely choose these things more carefully in the future.  I''m disappointed with the low score, but I hope to do better in the future.  Thank you for your defense of my shot!</td>', 'Originally posted by bohemka: I don''t know what blown highlights sldpixel is talking about. There are no blown highlights. And I don''t know what the problem is with there not being enough color... just because you called it Fall? I do agree the border is a bit weird though. Either go letterbox or equidistant all the way around (at least for voters); or better, no border at all, especially with a shot like this, which doesn''t need it. With a shot this good you want to go as big as possible, so scrap the border altogether. And a black border doesn''t help the scene. Sorry to go on about the border. It''s a great shot and should have done a hell of a lot better.   Thank you for the feedback, Scott.  I''m just getting into photography (bought my first DSLR 2 months ago) and I certainly appreciate all the critiques.  I thought I had a decent shot here, but it seems to have been dismissed for certain reasons.  Ultimately I made a poor decision with the title (hey I''m from Southern California, so this looks very much like fall to me), as well as the choice for a border.  Again, these are learning curves for me and I''ll definitely choose these things more carefully in the future.  I''m disappointed with the low score, but I hope to do better in the future.  Thank you for your defense of my shot!', '2010-10-08 21:23:45.000000', NULL, 0),
