(6189238, 912194, 113419, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>Truthfully, flower pictures aren''t my thing, but this one just jumped off the page at me!  It''s wonderfully done. <br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>the lighting on the flower totally makes it pop!  it just stands out from the bg which is equally as stunning<br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>n/a<br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>a beautiful artistic piece<br/>for a person who enjoys flower pictures this, I imagine, would be a stirring image<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>You placed in the top 20, you got 4 favs, you got great comments!  I mean what else is there?  Well, there are 2 suggestions....a slight crop at the top to remove the hot spot....and there is a little distracting white spot under the lilly pad, looks similar to a copyright symbol, that coulda been cloned out.  I know these are supposed to be in depth critiques, but how in depth can one go when the image is just on the verge of being perfect?  :-)</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club  First Impressions: Truthfully, flower pictures aren''t my thing, but this one just jumped off the page at me!  It''s wonderfully done.  Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): the lighting on the flower totally makes it pop!  it just stands out from the bg which is equally as stunning Challenge: n/a Artistic/Emotion: a beautiful artistic piecefor a person who enjoys flower pictures this, I imagine, would be a stirring image Summary: You placed in the top 20, you got 4 favs, you got great comments!  I mean what else is there?  Well, there are 2 suggestions....a slight crop at the top to remove the hot spot....and there is a little distracting white spot under the lilly pad, looks similar to a copyright symbol, that coulda been cloned out.  I know these are supposed to be in depth critiques, but how in depth can one go when the image is just on the verge of being perfect?  :-)', '2010-10-12 10:42:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6189303, 911609, 80908, '<td valign="top">Hi Kat, Welcome to the Critique Zone!<br/> <br/>My initial take on this is that it is a classic ''photograph'' - ie. ''writing with light''. There is no reliance on a pretty subject or fancy colours - this is a purists shot and a really nice example of one. Of course this means that it was never going to be a big hit with the voters in an FS, but I am sure you knew that and it is not your prime motivator! <br/> <br/><b>Technically</b>: You have gone for a pretty serious DOF with this, which works nicely, to capture the length of that shadow. That said, I would have found a slightly tighter focus on the chair more satisfying as a viewer, but that may just be me. The lighting, which this is all about of course, is excellent - all the more so since there is a hint of darkness about the photo as a whole.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b>: I like the concept of the composition, but the tilted line of the tarmac ''dip'' across the top is a little distracting. Ideally I would get rid of it, but if that''s not an option perhaps it could be level to add a sense of geometry? I also feel I would have liked to see the very end of the shadow, but again this might not have been physically possible.<br/> <br/>In summary, this is a fairly classic shot and I, for one, hope to see more of these on the site! Happy hunting.</td>', 'Hi Kat, Welcome to the Critique Zone! My initial take on this is that it is a classic ''photograph'' - ie. ''writing with light''. There is no reliance on a pretty subject or fancy colours - this is a purists shot and a really nice example of one. Of course this means that it was never going to be a big hit with the voters in an FS, but I am sure you knew that and it is not your prime motivator!  Technically: You have gone for a pretty serious DOF with this, which works nicely, to capture the length of that shadow. That said, I would have found a slightly tighter focus on the chair more satisfying as a viewer, but that may just be me. The lighting, which this is all about of course, is excellent - all the more so since there is a hint of darkness about the photo as a whole. Artistically: I like the concept of the composition, but the tilted line of the tarmac ''dip'' across the top is a little distracting. Ideally I would get rid of it, but if that''s not an option perhaps it could be level to add a sense of geometry? I also feel I would have liked to see the very end of the shadow, but again this might not have been physically possible. In summary, this is a fairly classic shot and I, for one, hope to see more of these on the site! Happy hunting.', '2010-10-12 11:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6189326, 911455, 113419, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>OH MY GOODNESS!  WOW!<br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>composition, lighting, color focus?  all magnificent!  If I were able to take these type photos I see nothing I would change <br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>n/a <br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>a piece that touchs us all on a level that we can understand - don''t disturb our rest!  very well excuted artistically and emotionally<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>A perfectly done animal portrait - can''t think of much more I can add - wish I could but this photo does it for me - no questions asked - no suggestions to be given</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club  First Impressions: OH MY GOODNESS!  WOW! Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): composition, lighting, color focus?  all magnificent!  If I were able to take these type photos I see nothing I would change  Challenge: n/a  Artistic/Emotion: a piece that touchs us all on a level that we can understand - don''t disturb our rest!  very well excuted artistically and emotionally Summary: A perfectly done animal portrait - can''t think of much more I can add - wish I could but this photo does it for me - no questions asked - no suggestions to be given', '2010-10-12 12:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
