(6191743, 912108, 113419, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>beatiful sunset, but what''s that thing in the lower left? (as you look at the picture)<br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>Beautiful subject, wonderful focus, great eye for color and a magficent capture; however I think the composition/lighting is off<br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>n/a <br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>artisticly, I can see that you were tying to capture the gorgeous curvature of the beach line<br/>emotionally, after I realize the whole scene I''d love to go for a walk on the beach<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>Maybe it was the darkness of the overall shot that kept you from a higher score, maybe it was the beach overpowering the shot; probably a combonation of the two.  Overall it''s a beautiful scene, however the eye is so drawn away from the sunset that it''s hard to know what your supposed to be looking at.</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club  First Impressions: beatiful sunset, but what''s that thing in the lower left? (as you look at the picture) Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): Beautiful subject, wonderful focus, great eye for color and a magficent capture; however I think the composition/lighting is off Challenge: n/a  Artistic/Emotion: artisticly, I can see that you were tying to capture the gorgeous curvature of the beach lineemotionally, after I realize the whole scene I''d love to go for a walk on the beach Summary: Maybe it was the darkness of the overall shot that kept you from a higher score, maybe it was the beach overpowering the shot; probably a combonation of the two.  Overall it''s a beautiful scene, however the eye is so drawn away from the sunset that it''s hard to know what your supposed to be looking at.', '2010-10-14 15:44:01.000000', NULL, 0),
