(6192323, 911990, 83313, '<td valign="top">You got robbed at gunpoint! I think it is a great capture of one detail of this ceremony. I gave this a 7. Guessing at why so many rated it low, I would think perhaps the person''s face being slightly turned away hurt it some, and it could probably do with a little pop and dimension. A mild amount of Topaz or PSP''s clarify would do it. (I don''t recall what you edit with). Hope that helps some. Now I will go read the other comments and see if they are in agreement with what I just said.<br/> <br/></td>', 'You got robbed at gunpoint! I think it is a great capture of one detail of this ceremony. I gave this a 7. Guessing at why so many rated it low, I would think perhaps the person''s face being slightly turned away hurt it some, and it could probably do with a little pop and dimension. A mild amount of Topaz or PSP''s clarify would do it. (I don''t recall what you edit with). Hope that helps some. Now I will go read the other comments and see if they are in agreement with what I just said. ', '2010-10-15 10:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6192324, 912236, 83313, '<td valign="top">I had thought this was yours because of the can''t-miss-it location printed in a "prominent place". That, and you were posting in the score thread that it was under a 5 at one point. Sports photography is not usually a mass appeal genre, but of all people on this site, you know what sells. I gave it a 7, however. I also gave the other cheerleader shot in this challenge an 8. Both are very good captures of a moment. I really like the use of blur to add to the action, even if it was merely a fortunate accident.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-15 09:10:07.</i></td>', 'I had thought this was yours because of the can''t-miss-it location printed in a "prominent place". That, and you were posting in the score thread that it was under a 5 at one point. Sports photography is not usually a mass appeal genre, but of all people on this site, you know what sells. I gave it a 7, however. I also gave the other cheerleader shot in this challenge an 8. Both are very good captures of a moment. I really like the use of blur to add to the action, even if it was merely a fortunate accident.', '2010-10-15 10:09:08.000000', '2010-10-15 10:10:07.000000', 0),
