(6192366, 912108, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Luci11e:</b></div><hr/><i> <b>Greetings From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>beatiful sunset, but what''s that thing in the lower left? (as you look at the picture)<br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>Beautiful subject, wonderful focus, great eye for color and a magficent capture; however I think the composition/lighting is off<br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>n/a <br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>artisticly, I can see that you were tying to capture the gorgeous curvature of the beach line<br/>emotionally, after I realize the whole scene I''d love to go for a walk on the beach<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>Maybe it was the darkness of the overall shot that kept you from a higher score, maybe it was the beach overpowering the shot; probably a combonation of the two.  Overall it''s a beautiful scene, however the eye is so drawn away from the sunset that it''s hard to know what your supposed to be looking at. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks a lot Lorie for your good and helpful critique, I think I agree with everything you say. <br/>All the best, Bragi (Brin)</td>', 'Originally posted by Luci11e: Greetings From the Critique Club  First Impressions: beatiful sunset, but what''s that thing in the lower left? (as you look at the picture) Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): Beautiful subject, wonderful focus, great eye for color and a magficent capture; however I think the composition/lighting is off Challenge: n/a  Artistic/Emotion: artisticly, I can see that you were tying to capture the gorgeous curvature of the beach lineemotionally, after I realize the whole scene I''d love to go for a walk on the beach Summary: Maybe it was the darkness of the overall shot that kept you from a higher score, maybe it was the beach overpowering the shot; probably a combonation of the two.  Overall it''s a beautiful scene, however the eye is so drawn away from the sunset that it''s hard to know what your supposed to be looking at.   Thanks a lot Lorie for your good and helpful critique, I think I agree with everything you say. All the best, Bragi (Brin)', '2010-10-15 11:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6192367, 910455, 69008, '<td valign="top">Nice shot Judi! I''m happy to see that you are getting out and about again and recovering from your fall.  <br/>The way you backlit parts of the rig and truck with flash, and painted the foreground for this make the shot for me.  That takes a lot of skill and a dash of good fortune to get it just right.  The WB is perfect in this too.  <br/>The Watson people should be very happy with this one. <br/>The star trails somehow remind me about you being dizzy for a while after the accident.</td>', 'Nice shot Judi! I''m happy to see that you are getting out and about again and recovering from your fall.  The way you backlit parts of the rig and truck with flash, and painted the foreground for this make the shot for me.  That takes a lot of skill and a dash of good fortune to get it just right.  The WB is perfect in this too.  The Watson people should be very happy with this one. The star trails somehow remind me about you being dizzy for a while after the accident.', '2010-10-15 11:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
